  "id": "COMPOUND:24565 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "Marsdenoside K is shown to have a target relationship with HepG2 through multiple pathways, with the core mechanism involving the inhibition of a target protein that ultimately leads to the suppression of HepG2 cell growth. The evidence is supported by the identification of SK-VLB, a protein that is targeted by Marsdenoside K and in turn targets HepG2. Similarly, VMRC-LCP, another target of Marsdenoside K, is also shown to interact with HepG2, suggesting a broader pathway of action. The presence of multiple targets that ultimately converge on HepG2 indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of cellular processes critical for the survival and proliferation of HepG2 cells. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link between Marsdenoside K and HepG2, with the observed scores reflecting the strength of the relationships. The evidence is consistent with a role in cellular signaling or metabolic pathways that are dysregulated in HepG2, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
